Not sure which is more Philly: the head coach ready to risk it all and fight a fan after a huge win. Or that an Eagles fan traveled all the way to Dallas, witnessed that miraculous win and then gave the coach the middle finger. Both things are  insane but I also love it.

One of the book ideas I have is “Explaining the Philly Fan” Which would be a look at the greatest moments of the insanity mixed w a deeper psychological and sociological study of the phenomenon. I’m gonna do it. Just a matter of when.

@intellivisi0x I saw similar w McNabb.  They would boo on 2nd down up 10 if throw was bad. Many such moments.

